{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_13852f3c2da46286bcb81fc0a43532735ff05b758365dce8e93ef9fc3b23efe8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8e1bcf46d536bd334df0b1882ca8c3554abefa57f31a75352ff7153067002aa3"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"Most findings are advisory: across the benchmark corpus 96.3% could not fail a build under the default policy, and outlier thresholds are per-repository so a clean check means only that nothing new was introduced.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_17ab7b4c5db75d06c2d0633b4b1556a4501c71674fda9031fb1b5f6bf2750457","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fafd1a4a987d5942857fdaad72d36fdf718f4acffa5b7b0dd2dd8ea3ea91a8a7"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"enola install --hooks writes instructions into agent-read files and adds hooks that grade each session; in opencode, which lacks such hooks, it installs a plugin that refuses the first grep/glob/list to surface the enola tool, bounded to two refusals.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_30381593ac7bd0fe372d626ab85d94466bb8cc2a44ab9803156e2b25d6b35329","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5a52b70e79bba53d2a0af04db076621f92ab733f174d268be67fb51474cfd50c","slc_c540f37a9b400f10980b8eabe85e83d636657848510a3834a106a8fae34b8f30"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"By default no policy is set: all findings are reported, the run exits 0, and the output explicitly states that nothing was enforced.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3abc2a8a413516a167aabdc54193d5aab26e3d7a57421fcd8a7febc94323827c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_484bd21196242af601349c7584222c3da0c1ecade348ec70414a1eeb31b10095","slc_596b81f5c574bf23901e0c306a023cc0dc774edc257a797ddd585f6bd4b661a4","slc_8920739bba01864bc5d453ac1a3c6c38256f469800eb5130c704e6d6dec455a1","slc_c92393097599357e747cd2cf224127b6177d61c87ee1ba00357587a7cb301b49","slc_d537f75d68d466674f1e2abdfe38d1dc769a3235cf997ddd1bbd0b96ed210ddb"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"The single binary is distributed via an install script, PyPI (enola-cli), Ruby gems, and package indexes, targeting Linux, macOS (amd64/arm64) and Windows without a Go toolchain or C compiler.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4036197ae948109e5e6509d36150809c5942d38b6720e970c93fdca589123429","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_57a0b65e3a98a8e9782d3ae2d0a85bcae539591177b1e59e91cbbf5077493f72","slc_9b071bcb83fd8aedd3224da30b78c206756051ef310227424475c4bba8389c0e","slc_f20e8455da5f7b74b93870a773cf48d5f31b5c8f922e2487036addcb8d9fe1f8"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"enola check uses four exit codes: 0 for pass, 1 for a failing finding or spillover, 2 for a missing baseline or bad flag, and 3 for a baseline incomparable to the current code.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4a37e51a604c5e223ed6909dfb7901109ace002c977661f5873a12a63de4d8eb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fafd1a4a987d5942857fdaad72d36fdf718f4acffa5b7b0dd2dd8ea3ea91a8a7"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"The install command previews every change and asks before writing, never creates shared files like AGENTS.md that did not already exist, and uninstall reverses everything byte-for-byte.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_542cd0352f1b9b0c46c3f159e8d17856e6d2fe06721e4ffc471826c38e28ce1d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0e75dd3dcdb85bbf083af7198e2104ac124fde94848b7f5ac6e9e3b250e8d124","slc_6333a8a966fc2aab743087a9a3f6378fa427ff8a9c62231caa60b2ece0fde133","slc_e2578161c5279d062ddd7a6b872efd64a7d65d5d7f6ba979fb88c7046915e181"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"Cross-repo analysis joins clients and services into one graph, resolving route prefixes interprocedurally across files and packages, and enola coverage reports per service how many outbound calls could not be matched to a route.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5a2f1a131fb798463a022fe9acde6cbd134976fa8cb43ff180e856cb224eb96f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2b1c535345cad7714df814ce2fc8d91ad7be85275ff4b45b933fc077241b9a59","slc_3edf12f6ed5881d1f2cdbf713d77fdd707754d8d89f14790b4a47b299773b2c1"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"Enola exposes itself to coding agents as an MCP server launched via the command 'enola', with per-client setup for Claude Code, Copilot, Cursor, opencode and Codex.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_65ae7c153485bac708252d00680e10c5267d22ed648d972211bafa6446dc65e7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8e1bcf46d536bd334df0b1882ca8c3554abefa57f31a75352ff7153067002aa3"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"Enola models only static structure and has no representation of runtime behavior such as timeouts, retry budgets, or message loss; the gate also grades only the delta, so pre-existing findings stay silent.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_65dddb94ae9f1f8264852000bc8570251295d5fab0a806088e5ac22dd0c748af","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03bbad7fccfdbba6a046544433e2b8b007634a65dc379a7efd6a1e6c6a19bb35","slc_972a03b1755d1a4b8b4b7807606c44ddc5827132da04b4d0c6a9e45e74a8a6bd"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"Snapshots carry a receipt with enola's version, git ref, dirty-tree status, extractors used, and a sha256-based snapshot ID; baselines pinned by a different version or ignore rules are deemed incomparable until re-pinned.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_70441d945b106704853d1f6b588ac9f195990c2555d0f6a9c4be6421c38850ec","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_29bcad1aefdb903545df321e547a36512f3aa9127042312022117f8f3795254a","slc_ed5f011e18ddb70cb477b243d246d6773c34edc7291eec94f4309fd2a9ff5b79"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"Enola targets AI-assisted development where agents write code faster than humans can review, catching structural regressions like layer violations and scope spillover that builds and tests miss.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_956ba2112f601871b425a5a32e040b1a049dd25f8f23105188bab4ceaee625a9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8e1bcf46d536bd334df0b1882ca8c3554abefa57f31a75352ff7153067002aa3","slc_c5e69e52c89c9e430f569c08cf4540073023d8a8ee592135d2e8b3e97c5d9ea1"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"Only cycles, intent, constraints and a declared layer order reach confidence 1.00; heuristic explainers are capped at 0.95, so gating on them requires lowering --min-confidence.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9f00cd44491716a4c0d31905d48cd028d4be5d145619c23e2d2757d24ab8cd73","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_36a6b8ea7f8b27a0c543118ff06c9b14a44beabd151078ce420610ebb6e9fcd4","slc_53216e909c664c2b9ce3cb40c3f256cd744afbfed7e59648d8e2b4419628894b","slc_ee948cf24482ea01c33fcb3513bc4db8d7d672511ceb4cf08a36218980256b30"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"Enola parses source with tree-sitter plus language-specific extractors, detecting 23 languages and formats automatically, with framework awareness for Go, Spring, Next.js, Angular, FastAPI, Django and others.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bbe9ee0411bc8f0bb1f7adfe65dbdba7ca9ba39ce08d8686aaafa0c0fad4e949","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_36a6b8ea7f8b27a0c543118ff06c9b14a44beabd151078ce420610ebb6e9fcd4","slc_53216e909c664c2b9ce3cb40c3f256cd744afbfed7e59648d8e2b4419628894b"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"The tool computes its graph from parsed source with graph algorithms, using no language model, embeddings, upload, account, or license check.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","created_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c4e8dffc705d6d5d9604455e4e8c6b1c83098d5d5907292a740affe97ccd3051","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"enola-labs/enola@f34e1998d5c4 snapshot 832a935ff1466519","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0396e99c9c2c915ad1dd285c182ead3fb771c7b6ede5b4d94bb5a2930340bbcc"],"source_ids":["src_1eced62061dc507897d6df530257edfe"],"text":"Enola maps a repository's structure before a change and compares it afterward, reporting only what that specific change introduced rather than pre-existing issues.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:08Z","updated_by_operation":"op_da24757a30a14e74aa77ce193315b5f9"}
